[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_1]
A Failed Diplomacy with Reindeers

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_1_desc]
Changeling Empire tried to convey the will of Queen Chrysalis to the reindeers: the reindeers must submit to the Changeling Empire and regularly pay love as tribute to the Changelings, otherwise the Changeling army will destroy Hailberg!
However, this diplomatic threat encountered an unprecedented failure: it was not that the reindeers dared to disobey the orders of the Changeling Empire, but that the orders of the Changeling Empire simply never reached the ears of the reindeers.
Our ambassador never succeeded in climbing the snow mountain, and was repeatedly driven back by blizzards, having to return to the camp. How did those things living on the snow mountain and the mountaintop manage to do it? It’s really puzzling.
Nevertheless, we have to find a way to make them submit to us, or at least hear us.

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_1_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_2]
The Ultimatum to the Reindeers

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_2_desc]
Correct answer: Use a balloon.

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_2_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_3]
Diplomatic Talks with Reindeers

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_3_desc]
Reindeers did not answer any of the requests made by our envoys at the talks, neither accepting nor rejecting. No matter how we threatened, they just kept talking about inexplicable prophecies and profound truths.
One of them, Alice, claimed to be able to predict the future. She warned our ambassadors, saying, “Our destinies are written in the stars.”
Then Alice explained that if we chose to use force, the conquest of the reindeers by the changelings would be successful, but the consequences would not be what the changelings wanted.

[en.EVENT_C11_MAIN_3_o0]
Turns out they’re just a bunch of lunatics

